<title>UK: MOTORCYCLING-WORLD SUPERBIKE CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-WORLD SUPERBIKE CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>DONINGTON PARK, England 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results</p>
<p>from the third round of world superbike motorcycling</p>
<p>championship on Sunday:</p>
<p>Race one (25 laps, 100.581 kms)</p>
<p>1. Aaron Slight (New Zealand) Honda  39 minutes 52.127 seconds</p>
<p>(average speed 152,899 kph)</p>
<p> 2. Carl Fogarty (Britain) Ducati	 39:53.810</p>
<p>3. Simon Crafar (New Zealand) Kawasaki 39:56.578</p>
<p> 4. Neil Hodgson (Britain) Ducati	 39:56.781</p>
<p> 5. Colin Edwards (U.S.) Yamaha	   40:01.475</p>
<p> 6. Scott Russell (U.S.) Yamaha	   40:02.865</p>
<p>Fastest lap: Pier-Francesco Chili (Italy) Ducati 1:34.723</p>
<p>Race two (25 laps)</p>
<p> 1. Fogarty				     39:48.996</p>
<p>(151.564 kph)</p>
<p> 2. Chili					 39:52.888</p>
<p> 3. Slight					39:53.133</p>
<p> 4. Crafar					39:55.376</p>
<p> 5. Jon Kocinski (U.S) Honda		39:57.211</p>
<p> 6. Edwards				     39:59.159</p>
<p>Fastest lap: Fogarty 1:34.637</p>
<p>Leading world championship standings:</p>
<p> 1. Fogarty	  110 points</p>
<p> 2. Slight	    99</p>
<p> 3. Kocinski	  96</p>
